# nauvis.surface: the surface of this run. Where the plots go is the world design, nauvis.fk; this
# file holds what is true of the world itself: the ground and how the game watches what is built.
# The base is one plot, and the kit and the reactor are part of its design (world.fk, kit.fk,
# plant.fk), so there is no claim to keep out of it: every tile inside the plot is yours.
surface  nauvis
# (3.1) `mode play` was here: a surface has properties now, and this one implied none
terrain  map                                    # map.terrain.json: the bare ground, read at kickoff
catalog  base
design   nauvis.fk                              # the plot: your world

watch plots:      keep
watch sanctioned: mark 2h
notify            nearby
